    "body": "I'm failing at doing the spec archaeology to understand why I thought this note was correct. I believe there was some specification text which supported this interpretation of how the cancel algorithm is invoked but I can no longer find it.  It's possible this was more strongly motivated by a quirk in the Chromium implementation rather than the specification as written.\n\nEither way, if the note is incorrect I think it can be removed because either behavior should be identical from a stream consumer perspective.",
